## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP over subsequences with a fixed length and pairwise costs, plus explicit reconstruction. It moves beyond contiguous partitions by requiring last-step linkage through prior picks.

## Key Concepts
- Subsequence DP with fixed length
- Min-over-predecessor recurrence
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and practical optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function solve(A, m){
  const n=A.length;
  const dp=Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(m+1).fill(Infinity));
  const par=Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(m+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[i][1]=0;
  for(let t=2;t<=m;t++){
    for(let i=t-1;i<n;i++){
      for(let j=t-2;j<i;j++){
        const c=dp[j][t-1]+Math.abs(A[i]-A[j]);
        if(c<dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=c; par[i][t]=j; }
      }
    }
  }
  let best=Infinity,bestI=-1;
  for(let i=m-1;i<n;i++){ if(dp[i][m]<best){ best=dp[i][m]; bestI=i; } }
  const path=[];
  let cur=bestI, t=m;
  while(t>=1){
    path.push(cur);
    cur=par[cur][t];
    t--;
  }
  path.reverse();
  return {cost:best, indices:path};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This gauges ability to cast a line-wrapping task into a clear 1D DP with a non-linear line cost and a reconstruction path. It tests handling of last-line quirks and feasibility checks.

## Key Concepts
- 1D DP over word indices; dp[n] = 0 as base.
- Prefix sums to compute line width in O(1) per extension.
- Cost function uses squared unused space; last line excluded.
- Reconstruct solution via next indices.
- Time: O(n^2); Space: O(n).

## Code Example
```javascript
function minWrap(words, W) {
  const n = words.length;
  const pref = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) pref[i + 1] = pref[i] + words[i];
  const dp = new Array(n + 1).fill(Infinity);
  const nxt = new Array(n).fill(-1);
  dp[n] = 0;
  for (let i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
      const width = (pref[j + 1] - pref[i]) + (j - i);
      if (width <= W) {
        const cost = (W - width) * (W - width) + dp[j + 1];
        if (cost < dp[i]) { dp[i] = cost; nxt[i] = j + 1; }
      } else break;
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return { minPenalty: dp[0], next: nxt };
}
```

